From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frank Liberato <liberato@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 16:22:34 -0700
Subject: Fix UAF in WebContentsImpl when dropping fullscreen for dialogs

When a JavaScript dialog, beforeunload confirm, or file chooser is
initiated, WebContentsImpl calls ForSecurityDropFullscreen() to exit
HTML fullscreen across related WebContents. Exiting fullscreen can
execute observers or dispatch events that destroy the initiating frame
(for example, if an iframe is removed from DOM).

When ForSecurityDropFullscreen() returns, WebContentsImpl accessed the
raw RenderFrameHostImpl pointer directly, resulting in a
heap-use-after-free.

This CL tracks the RenderFrameHostImpl using a base::WeakPtr across the
ForSecurityDropFullscreen() call in
WebContentsImpl::RunJavaScriptDialog,
WebContentsImpl::RunBeforeUnloadConfirm,
WebContentsImpl::RunFileChooser, and WebContentsImpl::ViewSource, and
aborts if the frame is destroyed or no longer active.

